        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_grants_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 77; } "The checker refuses exactly 77 corruptions before it checks anything generated. They are 42 records through the decoder, 10 weakened contracts and 4 contracts with an exclusive upper bound. They also include 2 drifted constants. The last 19 are binding files that differ from the rendered text by one edit. Four of those are read from disk as bytes. A dropped or invented control changes the count and re-admits the item.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-26d2-7653-924b-a3f113a718e6"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acad-760a-9132-5594ef107404"
      "The exam refuses a binding file that differs from the rendered text by one edit. The edits include a constant behind an attribute, in a comment or in a string. They also include a duplicate, an extra item, another value, another type, a missing header, CRLF line endings and a swapped pair. The exam also reads a file from disk as bytes. It refuses CRLF, a lone carriage return, a byte order mark and bytes that are not UTF-8."
      "Zenoh service grants: what each holder may publish and subscribe to"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_grants_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 77; } "The checker refuses exactly 77 corruptions before it checks anything generated. They are 42 records through the decoder, 10 weakened contracts and 4 contracts with an exclusive upper bound. They also include 2 drifted constants. The last 19 are binding files that differ from the rendered text by one edit. Four of those are read from disk as bytes. A dropped or invented control changes the count and re-admits the item.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-26d2-7653-924b-a3f113a718e6"; }; };
