    (h.req "01a1b49c-acad-760a-9132-55973870e3d7"
      "`just zenoh_grants_check` passes as the gate adapter observes it, and it fails naming the missing file until the generated constants land."
      "Zenoh service grants: what each holder may publish and subscribe to"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_grants_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-26d2-7653-924b-a3f113a718e6"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1 (done): Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table
    -- The Zenoh service has no way to receive its grants. The grants contract is a text record with no
    -- byte layout. The root serves a table to a component in whole rows through a window of fixed size.
    -- Without a table form, the next step has nothing to encode, serve or decode. Two readers would then
    -- each write the offsets by hand, and a misread layout would pass on both. This item fixes the table's
    -- layout, encodes it from a list of rows, and decodes it in Rust. A judge writes the same bytes again
    -- with Python's struct and compares all three.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed1f986d529b"
      "Eight row sets are each encoded to bytes equal to what `struct` writes from the pinned layout. They cover one publisher, a publisher and a subscriber of one key, and both rights on one row. They cover the longest and the shortest key and name. They cover rows given out of order, one holder on several keys, and a name of hyphens, underscores and digits. Each decodes back to its rows in table order."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 40; } "The checker counts 9 lines that the Rust test printed and 31 refusals by name. The 9 are the 8 honest tables and the closing line. The 31 are the corrupted tables the decoder refused. The total is 40. The count is exact. It is reported only after the judge accepted every line. The judge compares each line with bytes it wrote with struct and with its own decoder.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed20013facc6"
      "The Rust test decodes 39 tables the slice writes. The eight honest tables decode to the same rows as Python. The 31 corrupted tables are each refused. The test prints one line for each, and the judge compares the lines with its own."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 40; } "The checker counts 9 lines that the Rust test printed and 31 refusals by name. The 9 are the 8 honest tables and the closing line. The 31 are the corrupted tables the decoder refused. The total is 40. The count is exact. It is reported only after the judge accepted every line. The judge compares each line with bytes it wrote with struct and with its own decoder.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed21971955c0"
      "Rows are in strictly ascending order of holder name and then key, so a repeated pair is impossible. A table with two rows swapped, a row repeated, or the same key under the same holder with other rights is refused."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 40; } "The checker counts 9 lines that the Rust test printed and 31 refusals by name. The 9 are the 8 honest tables and the closing line. The 31 are the corrupted tables the decoder refused. The total is 40. The count is exact. It is reported only after the judge accepted every line. The judge compares each line with bytes it wrote with struct and with its own decoder.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed228c6e661b"
      "The encoder refuses 27 inputs. Some concern the rows as a whole: no rows, a row that grants nothing, and a repeated pair. Two concern the closed record: a field the grants record does not have, and a missing field. Some concern a holder name: zero bytes, 33 bytes, a capital, a dot, a space or a non-ASCII character. Some concern a key: zero bytes, 130 bytes, a star, a double star, a dollar or a question mark. A key may also hold a hash, a space or a non-ASCII character. Others are a leading, trailing or doubled slash, and rights that are not booleans."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 367; } "The checker refuses exactly 367 corruptions before it runs any Rust. Every field of every transcript line is changed alone, so a judge that stopped comparing one field fails. Four wrong decoders are written by name. One accepts a corrupted table, one refuses an honest table, one reads the rights swapped and one reads the rows reordered.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed23ceb5f8a0"
      "Over all 128 ASCII characters, the encoder accepts exactly the characters the grants contract lists as `nameChars` and `keyChars`. A character added to or removed from either list is refused by the judge."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 367; } "The checker refuses exactly 367 corruptions before it runs any Rust. Every field of every transcript line is changed alone, so a judge that stopped comparing one field fails. Four wrong decoders are written by name. One accepts a corrupted table, one refuses an honest table, one reads the rights swapped and one reads the rows reordered.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed24124d3358"
      "The committed `components/proto/src/zenoh_service_grants_table_wire.rs` equals the renderer's output byte for byte. Twelve edits are each refused. Some move an offset or change a length, a bound or the magic. Some narrow a field or drop a decode length check or an encode statement. Others remove the header comment or a trailing newline, add a line, or empty the file."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 367; } "The checker refuses exactly 367 corruptions before it runs any Rust. Every field of every transcript line is changed alone, so a judge that stopped comparing one field fails. Four wrong decoders are written by name. One accepts a corrupted table, one refuses an honest table, one reads the rights swapped and one reads the rows reordered.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed257439c003"
      "`components/proto/src/lib.rs` holds the two export lines once each, with no attribute directly above them. The Rust test imports the decoder through the crate, includes no source by path and reads the tables file the slice writes. Twenty-nine corrupted files are each refused."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 367; } "The checker refuses exactly 367 corruptions before it runs any Rust. Every field of every transcript line is changed alone, so a judge that stopped comparing one field fails. Four wrong decoders are written by name. One accepts a corrupted table, one refuses an honest table, one reads the rights swapped and one reads the rows reordered.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed26e0ba7b4a"
      "The slice runs the Rust test a second time on a file in which one honest table is replaced by another. A test that read the file prints the new table's line and no other line changes. A test that prints constants prints the first run's line again, and the slice refuses it. The judge refuses eleven wrong second runs, and the controls total counts them."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 40; } "The checker counts 9 lines that the Rust test printed and 31 refusals by name. The 9 are the 8 honest tables and the closing line. The 31 are the corrupted tables the decoder refused. The total is 40. The count is exact. It is reported only after the judge accepted every line. The judge compares each line with bytes it wrote with struct and with its own decoder.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed27a37b98ce"
      "The slice runs `every_table_decodes_to_its_rows_or_is_refused` alone with `--exact` and fails unless that test is the only one that passed and the target ran one test. Another test cannot supply the lines."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 40; } "The checker counts 9 lines that the Rust test printed and 31 refusals by name. The 9 are the 8 honest tables and the closing line. The 31 are the corrupted tables the decoder refused. The total is 40. The count is exact. It is reported only after the judge accepted every line. The judge compares each line with bytes it wrote with struct and with its own decoder.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed28a9405d67"
      "The schema's constants and both layouts are compared with a copy held in the judge. Each layout must add up to its size and list the fields of its record in order. Twenty-four edits to the schema are each refused. They change a constant, widen or reorder a field, or drop a field from only the layout or only the record. They also state a constant twice or add a line that is not a field."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 367; } "The checker refuses exactly 367 corruptions before it runs any Rust. Every field of every transcript line is changed alone, so a judge that stopped comparing one field fails. Four wrong decoders are written by name. One accepts a corrupted table, one refuses an honest table, one reads the rights swapped and one reads the rows reordered.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed29b7a0bdcf"
      "The judge refuses 367 corruptions before it runs any Rust. They are 24 schema edits, 27 refused inputs and 31 corrupted tables. They are also 4 alphabet edits, 4 encoder edits and 225 transcript edits. The last are 12 generated-file edits, 29 corrupted exports and 11 corrupted second runs. The judge fails if two controls of any kind share a label or corrupt the same input the same way."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 367; } "The checker refuses exactly 367 corruptions before it runs any Rust. Every field of every transcript line is changed alone, so a judge that stopped comparing one field fails. Four wrong decoders are written by name. One accepts a corrupted table, one refuses an honest table, one reads the rights swapped and one reads the rows reordered.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-add6-7514-a83e-ed2a92164e2e"
      "`just zenoh_service_grants_table_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter."
      "Encode, generate and decode the Zenoh service grants table"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_grants_table_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe fails until the generated file, the decoder and the test land.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18804-02b0-73f3-a2c8-1200b39844f1"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a (done): Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder
    -- The Zenoh service grants table has an encoder, and nothing calls it. The generation builder turns a
    -- system spec into a generation, and it has no step that builds the table from the grants a spec
    -- declares. Without that step, the table cannot reach the root. The first system spec to declare
    -- grants would also be the first test of the code that carries them. This item adds the builder step
    -- and the spec admission that runs it. It also adds a judge that grades both against the encoder's
    -- bytes and an independent writer.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfd-7183-9e8c-8df8f106c335"
      "From a manifest with three rows and a `zenoh-service` instance, the builder emits the bytes that `zenoh_grants_table.encode` emits. They equal the bytes that the table judge's struct writer emits, and they decode to the declared rows. Reversing the rows and the instances gives the same bytes."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 7; } "The checker counts seven checks that the builder's output must pass. Four compare the output with the encoder, with the independent writer, with a decode back to the rows and with a reversed order. Three follow a valid spec through admission. The count is exact. It is reported only after all seven held.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfd-7183-9e8c-8df936a1932e"
      "The builder refuses eleven manifests. Four concern the manifest: no rows, no reader instance, a holder that is not an instance, and the reader as a holder. Seven concern a row: it grants nothing, its key has a wildcard or is 130 bytes, or it repeats a pair. A row may also hold a field the grants record lacks, lack its key, or carry rights that are not booleans. Each is refused at the boundary that owns it."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_builder_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 14; } "The checker refuses exactly 14 inputs. Eleven are manifests and three are specs. Each names the boundary that must refuse it, so an input refused by another boundary fails the exam. A one-line mutation of each builder check was run against the slice. One removed check, the empty table, is also refused by the encoder, so removing it from the builder changes the message and not the verdict.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfd-7183-9e8c-8dfa2a85b707"
      "A real spec with a `zenoh-service` instance added and three grants set is admitted. The manifest it derives holds the three rows as declared and a `zenoh-grants` object. The table built from that manifest equals the encoder's bytes for the rows. A derivation that dropped every row, or kept only the first, fails the slice."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 7; } "The checker counts seven checks that the builder's output must pass. Four compare the output with the encoder, with the independent writer, with a decode back to the rows and with a reversed order. Three follow a valid spec through admission. The count is exact. It is reported only after all seven held.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfe-7113-80ba-20c4788e2131"
      "The system spec refuses three specs. They are grants without their object, a holder the spec does not admit and an object with no grants. The two new keys default in, so every existing spec is accepted as before."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
