    -- legacy 01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72 (done): Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record
    -- The generation builder encodes the Zenoh service limits record and never compares the rows with it.
    -- A manifest whose limits declare one holder, or short keys, is accepted beside rows that name more
    -- holders and longer keys. The service then serves more than the declaration says. This item plans the
    -- builder's checks and the exam that grades them. The exam fails until the implementation lands.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6abecf3591"
      "The builder emits the encoder's bytes for a manifest's limits. The exam requires the independent struct writer's bytes and a decode back to the declared limits, whatever order the rows and instances come in."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 13; } "The checker counts ${CASES} honest checks. Four are the record's bytes, three ways and one reorder. Six hold the limits at the rows. Three are exact. One has a key that is not subscribed, one has two holders on one key, and one has a stack below the executable's. Three are of the record a spec derives. A builder that emits other bytes or refuses at a limit fails.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6b53163abc"
      "The builder refuses rows that name more holders than the record declares. It refuses rows that subscribe to more distinct keys than it declares, or hold a key longer than it declares. The exam holds each limit exactly at the rows, and with a key that is published and not subscribed."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 13; } "The checker counts ${CASES} honest checks. Four are the record's bytes, three ways and one reorder. Six hold the limits at the rows. Three are exact. One has a key that is not subscribed, one has two holders on one key, and one has a stack below the executable's. Three are of the record a spec derives. A builder that emits other bytes or refuses at a limit fails.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6c18ed229a"
      "A spec that declares the service and its limits derives a manifest whose service instance holds the limits as declared and the object `zenoh-limits`. The record built from it equals the encoder's bytes."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 13; } "The checker counts ${CASES} honest checks. Four are the record's bytes, three ways and one reorder. Six hold the limits at the rows. Three are exact. One has a key that is not subscribed, one has two holders on one key, and one has a stack below the executable's. Three are of the record a spec derives. A builder that emits other bytes or refuses at a limit fails.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6d1cf6d094"
      "The exam refuses 15 manifests and 5 specs, and each refusal must come from the boundary that owns it. The refusal names its reason, and a refusal at another boundary fails the exam."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 20; } "The checker refuses exactly ${CONTROLS} inputs: 15 manifests and 5 specs. Each is applied alone, and the honest input is accepted first. The refusal must name the reason of the boundary that owns it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6e3059a9a7"
      "A composition with an instance named `zenoh-service` declares its limits. A spec without them is refused at admission."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 20; } "The checker refuses exactly ${CONTROLS} inputs: 15 manifests and 5 specs. Each is applied alone, and the honest input is accepted first. The refusal must name the reason of the boundary that owns it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6fb80479b3"
      "`just zenoh_service_limits_builder_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter. It fails on `main` until the implementation lands."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe passes only after the implementation pull request merges, because the full run reads the builder it names.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
  }) with {
    nonGoals = {
      "How the grants reach the service at run time. That is a list in the system spec, a generation resource kind, a root-served read and a decoder in the service. The component item owns it.";
      "The service core, the client interface and any Zenoh behaviour. The core item judges those against a record of this contract.";
      "Wildcard keys, key aliases, and a holder that names a topic and a type for the service to turn into a key. A grant is one exact full key.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR. The generated Rust file and the system-spec grammar belong to the implementation.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR.";
      "The read label, the manifest and system spec fields, the `slime-root` reader and the runtime wrapper. They change existing schemas and product code, so a planning PR cannot carry them. A later item owns them.";
      "The builder's use of the encoder. The encoder takes a list of rows, and this item does not wire it to a manifest field.";
      "The Zenoh service component and a booted composition.";
      "A change to `contracts/zenoh-service-grants/v1`. The record is landed. This item reads its alphabets.";
      "A row holder identity or a hash. The root serves the whole table to one named instance, so a row needs only the holder's name.";
      "Isolating two decoder guards. The row-count bound is reachable only by a buffer of 11 megabytes, and the total-length check refuses a header that claims more rows. The key-length guard is covered by the empty-segment check, because an empty key splits into one empty segment. Removing either guard changes no verdict the judge can show. Both stay in the decoder and are recorded as known limits.";
      "A system spec or a composition that declares grants. No composition has a `zenoh-service` instance, and the schema does not declare the two keys, so a `.zti` spec cannot carry them yet. A later item owns the schema fields.";
      "The read label, the manifest and system spec schema fields, the `slime-root` reader and the runtime wrapper. They change existing schemas and product code.";
      "A check that each holder has an endpoint to the service. The endpoint grants do not exist until the component does, so a later item owns it.";
      "A change to the `4096` object size the spec writes. Nothing checks it against a payload, and the table's size is its payload length.";
      "Adding the encoder and the table schema to the release inputs in `scripts/generate/generate-system-image-closures.py`. The builder runs `scripts/lib/zenoh_grants_table.py` and reads the table schema, and neither is a release input. The same holds for the entropy and network encoders in `scripts/build/generation_resources.py` and for `boot_contracts.py`. No composition declares grants, so no image can differ yet. A later item that enables a composition owns the release inputs for all of them.";
      "A change to the 363 tests that `just test_sel4_root` pins. CI runs that recipe, so raising the count before the tests exist would fail every pull request.";
      "A check that the two tests exercise the reader. The exam reads their names and counts from the run. Two empty tests with those names would pass. The implementation pull request is reviewed for that, and a checker-owned fixture would close it.";
      "The implementation. It is a separate pull request that carries every product change together, because `slime-root` cannot compile before the label exists in `slime-proto`.";
      "The documentation row for label 75 and the pin of 365. `check-syscall-abi` fails when the document and the contract disagree, and `just test_sel4_root` fails when the pin and the count disagree. Both land with the implementation.";
      "The ceiling entry in `scripts/lib/system_spec.py`. It reads a generated constant that does not exist until the schema declares it.";
      "A run of the reader through a booted root. No component reads the table, and the exam grades the reader by its host tests.";
      "A compile of the runtime wrapper. `just test_host` does not build that crate, so the exam reads the wrapper as text. The entropy wrapper is graded the same way.";
      "The Zenoh service component, its endpoint grants and a booted composition.";
      "Adding the encoder and the table schema to the release inputs. The decision record names this limit and a later item that enables a composition owns it.";
      "A third test. The exam requires exactly two. A test added later raises the count here and the pin in the same pull request.";
      "The system spec and manifest fields, the builder, the root's read, the service and the core. The implementation pull request adds them.";
      "A new version of the grants table. The record is separate so that the table and its 367 controls stay as they are.";
      "A syscall or a label. The record uses the cursor of the existing read, and the pinned wrapper in `syscall.rs` keeps its comment, which names the table version.";
      "The stack arithmetic. `zenoh-service-grants/v1` states it. The builder does not evaluate that contract, so the contract is not a generation input. The builder checks the stack against its own bound, and the service checks it against its storage.";
      "Holders other than the two the composition has. This item makes a larger table possible and does not add one.";
      "A test of the proto decoder, the core, the builder or the service. The implementation adds them, and its review checks that each one fails when the code is wrong.";
      "The builder, the spec derivation and the service. The implementation pull request adds them, and it is already written.";
      "The stack against the rows. The service checks the declared stack against the storage it was built with.";
      "What the service does with a limit above its ceilings, and what the root serves. The limits item and the implementation review own them.";
      "A mutation harness as a gate. The implementation pull request reports one run of it, and the exam is the gate.";
    };
  };

area
